Restore the original release's PRESS-only blocking input contract.

The March 2011 game shipped with a libtcod whose wait_for_keypress converts
SDL events with TCOD_KEY_PRESSED only.  The reused August 2012 1.5.1 tag's
legacy wrapper instead requests TCOD_EVENT_KEY (PRESS | RELEASE), despite
still documenting a wait for a key press.  Without this adaptation a normal
press/release tap can advance the game twice, including during targeting.

Use the public event API directly at all four original waits.  Keep each
original flush=true argument, initialize/reset the key to preserve the NONE
result on SDL_QUIT, and retain normal held-key repeat and all game actions.
The shared renderer and its other consumers are deliberately unchanged.

--- a/GodOfChange.cpp
+++ b/GodOfChange.cpp
@@ -390,7 +390,8 @@
          player.stuck = false;
          acted = true;
       } else {
-         TCOD_key_t key=TCODConsole::waitForKeypress(true);
+         TCOD_key_t key={TCODK_NONE,0};
+         TCODSystem::waitForEvent(TCOD_EVENT_KEY_PRESS,&key,NULL,true);
          int destx = player.x, desty = player.y;
          int testX = -1, testY = -1;
          if (key.vk == TCODK_ESCAPE) {
@@ -1118,7 +1119,8 @@
